---
name: container-gpu-errand-noble

description: |
  Errand that validates GPU access from inside a container on a BOSH-managed VM.
  Installs Docker and nvidia-container-toolkit, configures CDI mode, generates
  a CDI spec, and runs nvidia-smi plus a small CUDA workload in a container.

  Prerequisite: GPU-enabled stemcell (ubuntu-noble 1.365-nvidia) with the
  NVIDIA driver pre-baked. This errand does not install the driver itself.

  Usage:
    bosh -d container-gpu-test deploy bosh/gpu-test-release/manifests/container-gpu-test-noble.yml
    bosh -d container-gpu-test run-errand container-gpu-errand-noble

templates:
  run: bin/run

packages: []

properties: {}
